From 066d6802c351bee083b8f815f150c618295e46c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 03:28:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Rotation of all the tangent operator blocks of orthotropic
 behaviours

The rotation functions of the `generic` and `generic-parallel` interfaces
reported an error for the tangent operator blocks associated with arrays of
variables, with a vector and a symmetric tensor or a tensor, or with a
tensor and a symmetric tensor (TFEL has no `change_basis` for `st2tot2`).

- a block associated with arrays of variables is made of one sub-block for
  each pair of entries, stored contiguously: each sub-block is rotated;
- a block for which TFEL has no type which can be rotated is rotated by the
  new `mfront::gb::rotateTangentOperatorBlock` function, which computes
  Q1 K Q2^T, where Qi is the matrix of the rotation of the objects of each
  variable by `change_basis` (usable in device code);
- the other blocks are rotated as before (unchanged generated code).

The `OrthotropicTangentOperatorBlocksTest` behaviour has blocks of all
kinds; its rotation functions are compared by the generic-parallel tests.
